A||||20||Motorhead||ALCL diagnosis
Z||000000||Motorhead||05-13-99||02:01 AM||||In an attempt to further my education regarding this car of mine, I attempted code retrieval using the ALCL connector.<p>After thouroughly reviewing this procedure in the Haynes manual, I felt confident that I wasn't going to fry the ECM.<p>However, I found that when I grounded the dagnostic terminal,the only affect was continuous illumination of the upshift light.<p>Several things occured to me at this time.  <p>  1]  I've never seen this light illuminated<p>  2]  Which light on the dash is it?<p>  3]  Shouldn't it "test" illuminate prior to starting?<p>  4] Am I orienting the ALCL connector correctly with the diagram in the book? Is the diagram in the book actually upside down due to the fact that you allmost have to stand on you head while seated in the drivers seat?<p>I've vissually checked all the indicatr light bulbs and any fuses I thought might be relevant.<p>I understand from the descrip<br>tion in the book that the only thing that can illuminate this light, is a fault detection by the ECM, and after reviewing the electrical schematic, I can't seem to find any before start test circuite as on the other warning lights. Maybe I'm not reading this thing right!<p>Because of lack of time, and reluctance to screw around with the ALCL terminals for fear of damaging ECM, I quit, and buttoned everything back up.<p>Sorry for the long post, but I'm hoping one of ya'll can answer my questions.<p>As allways, thanks for the help!
Z||000001||Patrick||05-13-99||02:12 AM||||Hi Motorhead,<p>It's too late for me to get into this tonight, but if your <b>Upshift</b> light is illuminating, I'd say something is wrong.<p>It's supposed to be the <b>Service Engine Soon</b> light that flashes the codes.<p>If Ogre doesn't beat me to the punch, I'll have more to say about this tomorrow.<p>  
Z||000002||theogre||05-13-99||07:26 AM||||I'm bored this morning, so I'll beat him too it:) (slow week here.... starting to get realy tedious. I hope next weeks not the same.)<p>On one side of the connector there is a key. that's the row terminals A&B are on. I believe this connector is in the same orientation in all Fiero, so that makes A&B the 2 terminals on the lower row closest the pasenger seat the one you want to connect. The diagram below is as viewed from the front of the car.<p> |--------||AB------|<br>      | &lt;----Key<p>jump these 2 terminals, and turn the key to run. DO NOT try to start the car.<p>If your check engine light is working the first code is always the test patern code 12. each code will repeat 3 times. If code 12 flashes continuously there are no other codes.
Z||000003||theogre||05-13-99||08:16 AM||||the key in that diagram is in the center.... I forgot ultimate throws out lead spaces.
Z||000004||Motorhead||05-13-99||03:57 PM||||AHA! Then I was right!  Haynes' manual does depict the key on top, WHEN! In actuallity it is on the bottom! SOOOO! Standing on my head, I do, indeed have the correct terminals!  So why am I getting continuous illumination of the up-shift light, with no engine light?  And does this thing have a test circuit for illumination prior to start up?<p>I'm tellin' you, the guy that owned this car prior to me should be shot!  Forget the "make him dance routine"!<br>
Z||000005||theogre||05-13-99||06:54 PM||||check engine should light when the key is turned to start. if it doesn't check the bulb.
