Z||000009||Patrick||05-14-99||07:57 PM||||<br>Motorhead, what do you mean you "visually checked the bulb"? Why didn't you just swap the bulb with another one of the idiot lights that you knew worked?<p>Man oh man, I can see you're going to have fun this weekend! <IMG SRC="http://forums.gagames.com/forums/biggrin.gif"> <p>PS. By the way, when I mentioned that the my light was not connected, I meant it was no longer in place. I don't want you to think that there might be some way for the bulb to be "disconnected" when it's actually still in the instrument panel. Well, there might be a way to do that, but most people would just remove the bulb.<p>PPS. Ogre and I charge extra on the weekend. <IMG SRC="http://forums.gagames.com/forums/smile.gif"> <p><br>
Z||000010||Cliff Pennock||05-15-99||01:08 AM||||Actually, it used to read "<b>Check Engine Soon</b>", but for some reason they changed the text to "<b>Service Engine soon</b>" after the 86.5 model I think.
