Z||000016||GREENDANO||06-03-99||04:49 PM||||First things first, Cliff the reason it was changed from check engine is because people were calling dealerships/service stations and saying, "I checked my engine and it's still there"  If it said "service" people were more likely to get the car fixed.  (as per the government)  How many times at night have you passed a car with an orange glow from the dash.  (check/service light)?<br>  When I bought my car, the CEL was out.  When I took the dash cover off to check the bulb, the previous owner had broken off one tabs to keep the bulb out without having a missing bulb.  When I replaced the bulb, HEY whatdya know the CEL came on while driving.  It was to keep the bulb out while the used car sale was being made.  How do I know this you ask?  I know the guy who "broke" the bulb.  He told me this months later when I was talking to him.<br>  Live and learn....<br>  Dan-O
Z||000017||theogre||06-03-99||06:07 PM||||car sales are another reason to own your own ECM scanner. As soon as the lamp didn't light when the key was turned on, you could have scanned it. If they won't let you scan it you don't want it.
Z||000018||Motorhead||06-03-99||07:18 PM||||Ogre!  To be perfectly honest, The average used car salesman can't even spell scanner, let alone know what one is!  The ones I've met all seem to have some kind of learnig disability. Guess that's why they do what they do for a living!<p>If your forced to buy a used car on a lot, the first rule is:<p>I'm dealing with an IDIOT who knows nothing about this car!<p>Second rule;<p>Buy the car at the end of the month.  You'll get a better deal because the salesman is probably willing to cut commision to make their monthly quota.<p>Third rule;<p>Don't go for the "extra" warranty. Sales people get a very high commision on this "add on".<br>A dealer ain't gonna' offer this on a car he feels is going to break down as you pull it off the lot.  But he will offer it on a car that he thinks is in good enough shape to operate properly for the duration of the warranty he's trying to sell you.<p>Lastly!<p>Don't ever pay the initial asking<br> price!  The sales persons' commision is based on net profit, make that crook trying to sell you that car give up some money!<p>Can you tell that I was<br>married to a car salelady for longer<br>than I care to admit!<p>Sorry for the long post folks!!
